MausDroid is an Android adaptation inspired by and following the design of
OpenMausBot (https://github.com/milind-soni/OpenMausBot), Copyright Milind
Soni, Apache License 2.0. The Composio Tool Router Session approach, the
Claude Code / Codex permission-prompt-over-MCP approach and the SKILL.md
skills format follow OpenMausBot. OpenMausBot's `enterprise/` folder
(separately licensed) was not used.

Bundled third-party components:
- nodejs-mobile 18.20.4 (MIT and Node.js licenses) — JavaScript runtime
- Tailscale tsnet (BSD-3-Clause) — built-in Tailscale (tsbridge)
- Preact (MIT), qrcode-generator (MIT), NanoHTTPD (BSD-3-Clause), AndroidX (Apache-2.0)
- Sonic (Bill Cox, Apache-2.0, https://github.com/waywardgeek/sonic, commit b93885d) — per-phrase speed and pitch
- Spoken and written style adapted from Humanizer (Siqi Chen, MIT, https://github.com/blader/humanizer) the behuman skill (Alireza Rezvani / voidborne-d, MIT, https://github.com/alirezarezvani/claude-skills), talk-normal (hexie, MIT, https://github.com/hexiecs/talk-normal) and sustained-presence (claylo, Apache-2.0, https://github.com/claylo/sustained-presence)
- Voice timing patterns (tool preamble, micro-acknowledgement, backchannels while you talk) adapted from protoVoice (protoLabs, Apache-2.0, https://github.com/protolabsai/protoVoice)
- Speech: the phone's installed Phonon engine (gradium-ai/xn-ptts, MIT/Apache-2.0) through Android's text-to-speech service; no model is bundled
